{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum","id":1156665,"title":"[2E] Brother Clement \u2013 Nosferatu Methuselah from Lancea Sanctum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-07T07:06:37-08:00","id":1156665,"title":"[2E] Brother Clement \u2013 Nosferatu Methuselah from Lancea Sanctum","content":"I\u2019m preparing one of chronicle antagonist for my Werewolf game \u2013 ancient vampire from Middle Ages that hunt on descendants of Uratha that killed his Sire and \u2018brother\u2019 at times of Vikings. I have some questions about Methuselahs phenomena and would be glad for some guidance in NPC creation. I offer then sharing with ready ancient vampire to use in your games. \ud83d\ude09<br /> Questions on the start:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I understand that Methuselahs need their cycles of Torpor \u2013 and in those they come weaker, literary loosing Disciplines dot, yes? <b>So how those ancient vampires survive on \u2018night-to-night\u2019 basis in All Night Society?</b></li> <li>I want my Methuselah to return to All Night Society in modern Lancea Sanctum domain and pretend to be only Ancilla or Young Eldar, circa 200 years at most. <b>Is it possible with some powers or something like that? </b><b>Can any vampire just judge other Kinder age?</b></li> <li><b>What XP amount would be suitable for 1350+ years old vampire? </b>Shown in <i>Thousands Years of Night </i>100 XP seems like joke.</li> </ol>And now we go to the Brother Clement history...<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Brother Clement was one of first monks on Northern Scotland on Isle Iona that came in over one hundred years after Saint Columba mission. He was isolated servant of God because of his leprosy. In small colony he worked with those like him, copying holy manuscripts. Until came his Sire.<br /> <br /> Ambrosius was one of Nosferatu that remembered last days of Roman Empire. Or at least he thought he was. He was \u2018martyr\u2019, Dark shining example in the ways of Sanctified and Haunts for Clement. Hideous, terrifying, dark angel in immortal flesh. And then werewolves took Ambrosius from Clement.<br /> <br /> They came with Vikings. When pagans slaughtered the abbey, Raging wolves in threw human skin shredded his Sire and Mauris, brother in Ambrosius Blood. Clement survived only because his gift to Obfuscate. But then \u2013 seeing his \u2018father\u2019 and \u2018brother\u2019 ripped apart \u2013 he forsworn he will revenge on descendants of wolves that took them from him. Now, ancient monk comes to your city...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T07:40:49-08:00","id":1156678,"title":"","content":"First misconception: The vampire might lose Blood Potency, and augmented attributes and Skills above superhuman limits, but not discipline knowledge.<br /> <br /> Second: Barring witness recognition, elders are capable o adapting to the modern world, over and over, so that's entirely possible assuming the elder wants to resign to his rights within the organization.<br /> <br /> I don't know, 500xp? 1000? I wouldn't worry with the exact amount, just fill in the blanks as needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T08:14:00-08:00","id":1156686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1156678#post1156678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First misconception: The vampire might lose Blood Potency, and augmented attributes and Skills above superhuman limits, but not discipline knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if Methuselah get to Disciplines level 6+ he can have those even after Torpor time, yes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1156678#post1156678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second: Barring witness recognition, elders are capable o adapting to the modern world, over and over, so that's entirely possible assuming the elder wants to resign to his rights within the organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>So 1350+ years vampire can pretend to be like 200 years old only, something like made on early 1800's, yes? No other Kindred will not 'sniff' how old Methuselah is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T08:22:02-08:00","id":1156689,"title":"","content":"You're mixing VtR up with VtM. Disciplines cap at 5 dots. Additionally, I don't think 6+ Attributes and Skills are lost or suppressed even if the elder falls below 6 in BP in second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T08:50:01-08:00","id":1156700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1156689#post1156689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're mixing VtR up with VtM. Disciplines cap at 5 dots..</div> </div> </div> </div>Thousand Years of Night seems to point that you can have 'superDevotions' even if they use Disciplines from 1 to 5...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1156689#post1156689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, I don't think 6+ Attributes and Skills are lost or suppressed even if the elder falls below 6 in BP in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where should this info be in 2E corebook? Would check rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T09:01:04-08:00","id":1156705,"title":"","content":"But there's no rules that differs between regular devotions and so called elder devotions. They're all just devotions. It's just that older kindred tend to develop more powerful devotions since they have higher Disciplines and more XP.<br /> <br /> &quot;When her Blood Potency falls below six dots, the vampire does not lose any Attributes or Skills above the fifth dot.&quot;<br /> Last sentence on page 89.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T12:06:57-08:00","id":1156755,"title":"","content":"1. They survive the same way as any other vampire.<br /> 2. A Mekhet using Auspex to ask the question. &quot;How old is this vampire?&quot; Will yield the correct answer. Especially if this Brother Clement character is lying about it or trying to keep it secret. <br /> 3. Build the character and total the XP afterwards. Then look at it a week later and see if there's some merits, attributes , skills you can pare back and do it. Tally the modified character's XP expenditure then shave off another 15% Xp from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T12:29:20-08:00","id":1156763,"title":"","content":"As others have said, but to recap a bit:<br /> <br /> 1. Blood Potency is reduced through Torpor. This is a benefit and a drawback. All other Disciplines, Skills, and Attributes remain the same. Merits (especially social merits) may suffer from being ignored. Obviously mortal touchstones will need to be re-established. Thousand Years (or the main book, I disremember) point out that ghouls cannot be used as touchstones--which is a contradiction from other presentations of them. Decide how you like it.... Personally I like ghouls as touchstones, but you could charge a small merit tax to do so, for example.<br /> <br /> 2. Torpor in 1e VtR was terrifying and to be avoided: a penalty for aging. In 2e it's a refreshing pause and many elders look forward to re-inventing themselves as vibrant members of the Danse after a century or so. They may even relocate, assume new identities and otherwise ditch their past live(s) to make the break cleaner. Listen to the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FywSzjRq0e4\" target=\"_blank\">Johnny Cash cover of &quot;Hurt&quot;</a> and you have the attitude of an elder contemplating torpor. <br /> <br /> 3. Elder Devotions are not clearly &quot;elder&quot;... it's a bit of a failing of the book, really. On this note, if the character wants to conceal his age and sneak around domains looking for werewolves he might develop a simple Devotion that obfuscates his past from Auspex: either making such questions come up blank or having a &quot;persona&quot; that he sets and Auspex returns, subject to a clash of wills test.<br /> <br /> 4. But generally speaking on the XP side, consider how active a character was during a given period of time, especially in learning new things and subjecting themselves to danger. An elder who just naps and wakes up to re-assume the reigns of power (looking at you, Invictus Ventrue!) isn't going to learn much from each cycle--the suggest XP in the book is probably sufficient. Someone who literally travels the world and can honestly answer to being from &quot;lots of different places&quot; with his funny polyglot accent probably has several times the suggested amounts. --It's your call. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T18:07:54-08:00","id":1156849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1156763#post1156763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Torpor in 1e VtR was terrifying and to be avoided: a penalty for aging.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's still not great \u2014 falling into torpor with any frequency effectively caps your Humanity at 5, and falling into torpor for long enough to shed Blood Potency remains a problem for detachment in and of itself until you hit Humanity 3; you can get around both of those limits by taking banes, but you only get so many of those. There are elders with the capacity to relish the chance for reinvention because the vast majority of elders are desensitized to the alienating effects of torpor outside the context of complete culture-shock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T23:39:28-08:00","id":1156913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1156763#post1156763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On this note, if the character wants to conceal his age and sneak around domains looking for werewolves he might develop a simple Devotion that obfuscates his past from Auspex: either making such questions come up blank or having a &quot;persona&quot; that he sets and Auspex returns, subject to a clash of wills test.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>So let's make those Devotions - one for 'blank' answer and second for 'I choose my answer cause I'm so great' one. I suspect both will be based on Obfuscate and Auspex, yes?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1156763#post1156763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. But generally speaking on the XP side, consider how active a character was during a given period of time, especially in learning new things and subjecting themselves to danger. An elder who just naps and wakes up to re-assume the reigns of power (looking at you, Invictus Ventrue!) isn't going to learn much from each cycle--the suggest XP in the book is probably sufficient. Someone who literally travels the world and can honestly answer to being from &quot;lots of different places&quot; with his funny polyglot accent probably has several times the suggested amounts. --It's your call.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>For ease of discussion - let's assume Brother Clement goes for cycles of 200 years. </b>Being Embraced in circa 650 A.D., his Sire and 'brother' being slain in 800 A.D., he run and gone to nap circa 820 A.D - from then on circle is set. So he wakes up in 1020 A.D., then is active up to 1220 A.D., then goes to sleep until 1420 A.D. to wake up, goes to sleep around 1620 A.D., wakes up in 1820 A.D. and is active last 200 years, again. He looks to fulfill his vow, until he goes to sleep in 2020 A.D. now. How this would repercus on his XP pool?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1156849#post1156849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's still not great \u2014 falling into torpor with any frequency effectively caps your Humanity at 5, and falling into torpor for long enough to shed Blood Potency remains a problem for detachment in and of itself until you hit Humanity 3; you can get around both of those limits by taking banes, but you only get so many of those. There are elders with the capacity to relish the chance for reinvention because the vast majority of elders are desensitized to the alienating effects of torpor outside the context of complete culture-shock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you explain more this Humanity problem with 200 years Torpor in mentioned above cycles? On what pages of 2E VtR corebook it is pointed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T07:51:00-08:00","id":1157005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1156913#post1156913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So let's make those Devotions - one for 'blank' answer and second for 'I choose my answer cause I'm so great' one. I suspect both will be based on Obfuscate and Auspex, yes?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Let's make this simple:<br /> <br /> <b>Cloak of Ages </b>[Merit **, supernatural]<br /> When the vampire uses <i>The Familiar Stranger</i> he may define at the same time as his appearance elements of his backstory that will be visible to cursory interrogation by Auspex. For example he may disguise himself as &quot;a sickly middle-aged plumber from Toledo with a history of bad marriages&quot; instead of &quot;a frail man&quot;. Any failure to overcome the vampire's Obfuscate through an Auspex Clash of Wills becomes a Dramatic Failure and provides impressions based on the false persona assumed. As with <i>The Familiar Stranger</i> the vampire has limited control over how others perceive him and cannot use the power to directly influence their thoughts and emotions. <br /> <br /> After a review, you could perhaps adapt a Devotion based on Obfuscate 2, Auspex 1 to blank out a vampire's background, but it would be somewhat obvious to an Auspex user (&quot;you get ... nothing... it's like he was born this night&quot;) and tend to create as many questions as the solutions it addresses. My recommendation is to go with the above merit, which shouldn't be any more powerful than Swarm Form as 2-dot merits go.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T09:30:36-08:00","id":1157028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1156913#post1156913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you explain more this Humanity problem with 200 years Torpor in mentioned above cycles? On what pages of 2E VtR corebook it is pointed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sample Breaking Points chart on page 107. &quot;Falling into torpor&quot; is a breaking point at Humanity 6 or above, and &quot;Spending a year or more in torpor&quot; is a breaking point at Humanity 4 or above. Per the Humanity Scale breakdown on the preceding page, most elders are going to have reduced their Humanity to the point of being Callous, which leaves the primary concern of torpor for their Humanity as the Humanity 2 &quot;Seeing a culture that didn't exist when you were alive&quot; breaking point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T09:47:56-08:00","id":1157033,"title":"","content":"There's also surviving a century at Humanity 4, surviving 500 years at Humanity 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:10:31-08:00","id":1157043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1157005#post1157005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's make this simple:<br /> <br /> <b>Cloak of Ages </b>[Merit **, supernatural]<br /> When the vampire uses <i>The Familiar Stranger</i> he may define at the same time as his appearance elements of his backstory that will be visible to cursory interrogation by Auspex. For example he may disguise himself as &quot;a sickly middle-aged plumber from Toledo with a history of bad marriages&quot; instead of &quot;a frail man&quot;. Any failure to overcome the vampire's Obfuscate through an Auspex Clash of Wills becomes a Dramatic Failure and provides impressions based on the false persona assumed. As with <i>The Familiar Stranger</i> the vampire has limited control over how others perceive him and cannot use the power to directly influence their thoughts and emotions.<br /> <br /> After a review, you could perhaps adapt a Devotion based on Obfuscate 2, Auspex 1 to blank out a vampire's background, but it would be somewhat obvious to an Auspex user (&quot;you get ... nothing... it's like he was born this night&quot;) and tend to create as many questions as the solutions it addresses. My recommendation is to go with the above merit, which shouldn't be any more powerful than Swarm Form as 2-dot merits go.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it - but why 'blank' power would be Devotion and <i>Cloak of Ages </i>is simple Merit? I do not understand reasoning here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T06:13:48-08:00","id":1157261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1157043#post1157043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like it - but why 'blank' power would be Devotion and <i>Cloak of Ages </i>is simple Merit? I do not understand reasoning here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because of the foci of the base powers/Obfuscate dot levels.<br /> <br /> The Familiar Stranger, core, is about disguising yourself as something you're not. Disguising your history at the same time is a natural extension of it in much the same way that Swarm Form is a natural extension of Protean 3. You don't need a new, separate power to extend an existing one like that, doing the same thing in a slightly different way or area. Compare with, for example Claws of the Unholy, which does a <b><i>new </i></b>thing--inflict Agg damage--and therefore is a Devotion. The line is fine, but I think we're good.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Obfuscate at lower levels is about you or your target (objects and then other people) not being noticed, about them being either there (power off) or not-there (power on). A &quot;blank&quot; power to do that to a non-material thing (&quot;my background&quot;) targets a totally different area and is conceptually something you'd use while being otherwise noticed. In other words, you'd need a switch to take Obfuscate 2 and apply it to either self or self's background--which tells me we're dealing with a Devotion here. Further, the desired effect is one that should demand a Vitae expenditure.<br /> <br /> Iterative extension of effect? Potential merit.<br /> Retargeting of similar effect/Vitae cost? Potential Devotion.<br /> <br /> YMMV of course. Ultimately it's semantics: the player (or NPC) pays an XP cost that's similar and get the desired effect. And, in both cases, the development of the ability is one that would take in-game effort and a certain adaptation and story behind it.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T07:14:00-08:00","id":1157270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum#post1156665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m preparing one of chronicle antagonist for my Werewolf game \u2013 ancient vampire from Middle Ages that hunt on descendants of Uratha that killed his Sire and \u2018brother\u2019 at times of Vikings. I have some questions about Methuselahs phenomena and would be glad for some guidance in NPC creation. I offer then sharing with ready ancient vampire to use in your games. \ud83d\ude09<br /> Questions on the start:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I understand that Methuselahs need their cycles of Torpor \u2013 and in those they come weaker, literary loosing Disciplines dot, yes? <b>So how those ancient vampires survive on \u2018night-to-night\u2019 basis in All Night Society?</b></li> <li>I want my Methuselah to return to All Night Society in modern Lancea Sanctum domain and pretend to be only Ancilla or Young Eldar, circa 200 years at most. <b>Is it possible with some powers or something like that? </b><b>Can any vampire just judge other Kinder age?</b></li> <li><b>What XP amount would be suitable for 1350+ years old vampire? </b>Shown in <i>Thousands Years of Night </i>100 XP seems like joke.</li> </ol>And now we go to the Brother Clement history...<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Brother Clement was one of first monks on Northern Scotland on Isle Iona that came in over one hundred years after Saint Columba mission. He was isolated servant of God because of his leprosy. In small colony he worked with those like him, copying holy manuscripts. Until came his Sire.<br /> <br /> Ambrosius was one of Nosferatu that remembered last days of Roman Empire. Or at least he thought he was. He was \u2018martyr\u2019, Dark shining example in the ways of Sanctified and Haunts for Clement. Hideous, terrifying, dark angel in immortal flesh. And then werewolves took Ambrosius from Clement.<br /> <br /> They came with Vikings. When pagans slaughtered the abbey, Raging wolves in threw human skin shredded his Sire and Mauris, brother in Ambrosius Blood. Clement survived only because his gift to Obfuscate. But then \u2013 seeing his \u2018father\u2019 and \u2018brother\u2019 ripped apart \u2013 he forsworn he will revenge on descendants of wolves that took them from him. Now, ancient monk comes to your city...</div> </div> </div> </div>I quote in everything Khanwulf and I'd llike to point oit that torpor is not a needing in 2ed (and it just lowers the BP not the skills or disciplines). There are several way for an ancient to feed himself. <br /> Torpor COULD be a needing if you think about how BORED a Mathuselah can be of its life but it's more a flavor aspect then a fact <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Even because 450 years are enough to reach BP 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T07:47:21-08:00","id":1157280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1157270#post1157270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I quote in everything Khanwulf and I'd llike to point oit that torpor is not a needing in 2ed (and it just lowers the BP not the skills or disciplines). There are several way for an ancient to feed himself.<br /> Torpor COULD be a needing if you think about how BORED a Mathuselah can be of its life but it's more a flavor aspect then a fact <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Even because 450 years are enough to reach BP 10.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's kinda confusing to tell whom you're directing your comment to Marcus, but I'll pick up the torch of torpor and feeding for a moment to wave it too:<br /> <br /> Torpor as a fix to BP feeding issues is needed only if your vampire elder has disregarded his mystical side strongly in favor of mortal manipulations. There are many ways to get around feeding restrictions at this point, and latitude to develop more (&quot;I eat dreams&quot;, &quot;I consume your willpower in each delicious tear&quot;, &quot;I invade the spirit world and consume its essence!&quot; and etc...).<br /> <br /> Of course, down-to-earth vamps won't be doing any of these. They're rolling in issues related to politics, domain management, and the content battle to keep jealous underlings from burning their haven. It's distracting, to be blunt, and also the core assumption of VtR for <b><i>most</i></b> of its denizens. That's fine--no complaint.<br /> <br /> Where both your mystical and mundane vamps will get into trouble, however, is Languid. That condition is nasty and will drag a high-BP down the road to torpor pretty quick. The solution of &quot;don't lose your Touchstone&quot; is all fine and good until an enemy figures you out--then you have a big problem and an in-character shock coming with serious mechanical side-effects. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T18:49:12-08:00","id":1188739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1157280#post1157280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where both your mystical and mundane vamps will get into trouble, however, is Languid. That condition is nasty and will drag a high-BP down the road to torpor pretty quick. The solution of &quot;don't lose your Touchstone&quot; is all fine and good until an enemy figures you out--then you have a big problem and an in-character shock coming with serious mechanical side-effects.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting question - <b>Could your <i>enemies</i> be counted as Touchstones?</b> Like in Brother Clement example - he hunts all werewolves from the bloodline of murderers of his Sire and 'brother'. None the less those werewolves are reminding him about his life, don't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T18:54:02-08:00","id":1188743,"title":"","content":"General problem - <b>How Brother Clement should react to finding his werewolves targets? </b>He clearly have very high Obfuscate and Auspex, some dots in Nightmare and Vigor. <b>How would vampire like this 'hunt' on his targets?</b> Should he try even to kill wolves on start - instead, maybe, I don't know, crumble their position? Is there are some canons of Medieval Lancea Sanctum on relation with werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T06:59:12-08:00","id":1188859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1188739#post1188739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting question - <b>Could your <i>enemies</i> be counted as Touchstones?</b> Like in Brother Clement example - he hunts all werewolves from the bloodline of murderers of his Sire and 'brother'. None the less those werewolves are reminding him about his life, don't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer: yes. Longer answer: technically anything that's not a vamp could be a touchstone regardless of what that person thinks of the vamp--it's the meta-level of player versus character going on. Sure you hate your rival's guts, but they spur you on to greatness and given the opportunity to just off them you'll hesitate and rationalize your way out of doing so.<br /> <br /> A character like Brother Clement might even <i>shepherd </i>his werewolf targets/pack/lineage through the ages, ensuring that they have opportunities to rise to the occasion of being his prey. Because, yaknow, nothing is so unsatisfying as hunting down dangerous creatures and discovering they're as threatening as a Saltine cracker. They might not even realize who or what he is until he lets them or they gain enough power to figure it out... knowledge can be deadly, after all.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile he gets his touchstone connectivity fix.<br /> <br /> I'm entertained by this conversation because I'd already planned on setting up a similar scenario for a PC: they get an especially hardy vamp who takes him involuntarily as a touchstone, and therefore doesn't really want to kill him (or, let him be killed), even as the PC's mortal goals conflict with those of the vamp. Eventually, of course, the toy will get broken and they'll both need to sort out a new relationship.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 02-23-2018, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T09:15:13-08:00","id":1189605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1157261#post1157261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare with, for example Claws of the Unholy, which does a <b><i>new </i></b>thing--inflict Agg damage--and therefore is a Devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claws of the Unholy is a merit, not a devotion.<br /> <br /> On the topic itself - I'd make it a merit, which would invokve a clash of wills between one's obfuscate and Auspex to hide the true facts of his identity. Should he clash exceptionally, then eh can feed his own information to the Auspex user.<br /> <br /> as for touchstones: Their pirmary reason is to remind you how you're human. With Clement one could probably bend the &quot;vengeance is human&quot; bit to satisfy it for werewolves, but to me personally &quot;I, an ancient monster, hunt down werewolves, and thus remember better how to be human&quot; is a bit of a stretch. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T09:15:13-08:00","id":1189606,"title":"","content":"Edit/Double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 02-26-2018, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T12:47:59-08:00","id":1189667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1189605#post1189605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Claws of the Unholy is a merit, not a devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obvious embarrassing hole in argument is obvious. In my defense I have caught myself confusing Claws of the Unholy with the DA:Vampire/WoD Multi-Discipline power (Devotion) that does something virtually identical. So yeah, CotU is to me one of those points that wander for me in the grey area between &quot;solid Merit&quot; and &quot;solid Devotion&quot;; I should stay away from it.<br /> <br /> My more recent mental benchmark really boils down to &quot;how much should the power/ability cost in XP&quot;--especially if you just assume everything is supernatural somehow (even if not labeled as such). The differences being that Merits are 1 XP per dot (plus any potential prereqs), while Devotions have a formula for their cost that may make them more expensive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1189605#post1189605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic itself - I'd make it a merit, which would invokve a clash of wills between one's obfuscate and Auspex to hide the true facts of his identity. Should he clash exceptionally, then eh can feed his own information to the Auspex user.<br /> <br /> as for touchstones: Their pirmary reason is to remind you how you're human. With Clement one could probably bend the &quot;vengeance is human&quot; bit to satisfy it for werewolves, but to me personally &quot;I, an ancient monster, hunt down werewolves, and thus remember better how to be human&quot; is a bit of a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something to be said for interacting with/observing other monsters as they struggle to be &quot;human&quot;. Just hunting them down and killing them would not, I think, be sufficient (and would quickly detach your touchstone, since it shouldn't be &quot;werewolf hunting&quot; (an action) but could be &quot;werewolves of the line/pack of X&quot;). There's something to be said for expressing vengeance and the defense of humans as a part of your relationship with the werewolves as a Touchstone, based again on the humanness of such expressions.<br /> <br /> Again, if you're <i><b>just</b></i> going out and fighting/killing them, that's not really a meaningful interaction with your touchstone, IMO. There has to be more context behind it. All this is subjective, however, and I'd want to look deeper at a play who proposed such a touchstone to understand what his point really was--is there an effort to evade roleplaying and bone up on conflict at work?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T00:31:43-08:00","id":1189800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1189667#post1189667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something to be said for interacting with/observing other monsters as they struggle to be &quot;human&quot;. Just hunting them down and killing them would not, I think, be sufficient (and would quickly detach your touchstone, since it shouldn't be &quot;werewolf hunting&quot; (an action) but could be &quot;werewolves of the line/pack of X&quot;). There's something to be said for expressing vengeance and the defense of humans as a part of your relationship with the werewolves as a Touchstone, based again on the humanness of such expressions.<br /> <br /> Again, if you're <i><b>just</b></i> going out and fighting/killing them, that's not really a meaningful interaction with your touchstone, IMO. There has to be more context behind it. All this is subjective, however, and I'd want to look deeper at a play who proposed such a touchstone to understand what his point really was--is there an effort to evade roleplaying and bone up on conflict at work?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>So if Clement want's to 'play with a food' ( i.e. werewolves ) that still could be Touchstone? Just killing the outright would be only Aspiration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T03:11:13-08:00","id":1189819,"title":"","content":"I believe the interactions need to be portrayed in a humane fashion. If he thinks of a touchstone as mere food, it's not a touchstone to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T06:29:00-08:00","id":1189852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1189800#post1189800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if Clement want's to 'play with a food' ( i.e. werewolves ) that still could be Touchstone? Just killing the outright would be only Aspiration?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCorrect, up to a point (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a>' point, to be exact): destroying a group, or even a person, would be an Aspiration. Recognizing the essential humanity struggling within werewolves, and identifying with their challenge of balancing the monster and the man, would enable him to take a given werewolf, or even a pack, as a touchstone. <i>He can still have an antagonistic relationship with them</i>, however the character of that antagonism changes from extermination to... something else; perhaps something paternalistic, or authoritative, or sporting, or even competitive.<br /> There's a gulf of difference between &quot;I hate you and want you dead&quot; (which is straightforward, sensible and simplistic to an inhuman degree) and &quot;I hate you and making you suffer and struggle gives me meaning.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, even, &quot;I hate you and my hating you makes me human--so don't stop, don't fail... don't fall, because then on the precipice of that storm-lost time, what will I become without hate?&quot;<br /> <br /> Alternatively, my cat has an interaction with the field mice in the backyard (roughly a dozen interactions a year, on average), but they are not <i>meaningful</i> interactions. He forms no relationship with each mouse beforehand; there is no period of introduction. He enjoys hunting them until they break (which doesn't take long given he's proportionately the size of an apartment building); and he gets Willpower for indulging his Vice... or Virtue, depending on your point of view. Yet, he goes out several times a day to surveil the holes and watch over them. He probably took &quot;mouse holes in the back yard&quot; as his Touchstone, and interacting with them like a tiger in the jungle prowling water holes reminds him of his primal cat-ness.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 02-27-2018, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T13:17:52-08:00","id":1189987,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> False equivalence fallacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T14:04:48-08:00","id":1189997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1189987#post1189987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> False equivalence fallacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you complaining about my cat analogy? If so, know it's intended to be ludicrous, not the least because cats are not human and do not interact with their environment in human ways (especially not ones governed by VtR mechanics). Neither are vampires human, though it's a matter of arguable degree and wholly up to presentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T15:23:52-08:00","id":1190025,"title":"","content":"I would tend to agree that all touchstones do have to &quot;anchor&quot; you. Mindless hunting won't work. But stalking them, reminding werewolves of what kind of monster they are (which also keeps you in the perspective of what kind of monster YOU are) can serve as a touchstone. Like.. stalk them. If they are good people, warn them to &quot;keep your beast in check&quot;. If they are murderers, remind them of the harm they cause to people. If t heyre struggling in the middle, help them be better. That, I would count as a touchstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T17:13:10-08:00","id":1190071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156665-2e-brother-clement-\u2013-nosferatu-methuselah-from-lancea-sanctum?p=1189997#post1189997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you complaining about my cat analogy? If so, know it's intended to be ludicrous, not the least because cats are not human and do not interact with their environment in human ways (especially not ones governed by VtR mechanics). Neither are vampires human, though it's a matter of arguable degree and wholly up to presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was their morality again? Lemme check my book real quick: Oh, right. Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T21:55:48-08:00","id":1190140,"title":"","content":"Errr... the Humanity entry itself would like a word, friend?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR 2e, page 106</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred are not human. They were, once, but now they\u2019re something entirely different.<br /> [...]<br /> <b>Ascetic (Humanity 9-10):</b> [...] she\u2019s an expert in the way humans behave, feel, and think. She manages to think and act the way they do, <b>in the way an expert method actor would.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Emphasis mine, not the book's)</span><br /> <br /> I mean granted, because they <i>were</i> human the cat comparison doesn't work perfectly (unless Khanwulf's cat is secretly a human cursed to take the form of a housecat?). Thing with analogies though, is that they usually aren't one-to-one, <i>especially</i> intentionally-silly ones.<br /> <br /> ... Although, if we <i>do</i> try to treat the cat-watching-the-mouse-holes thing in game terms, it probably wouldn't make a half-bad Simulacrum Touchstone of sorts...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}